## Environment
Expected variables include:
`WORDPRESS_URL`, `WORDPRESS_USERNAME`, `WORDPRESS_APPLICATION_PASSWORD`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, optional `GEMINI_MODEL`, optional `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_GBP_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_GBP_REFRESH_TOKEN`, `GOOGLE_GBP_ACCOUNT_ID`, `GOOGLE_GBP_LOCATION_ID`, and optional `MOCK_GEMINI`.

**Secrets stay local. Never commit API keys, OAuth secrets, refresh tokens or WordPress application passwords.**

## WordPress Integration
Used endpoints include:
- `/wp-json/wp/v2/posts` — create blog drafts
- `/wp-json/wp/v2/media` — upload featured images
- `/wp-json/wp/v2/product_cat` — find relevant categories
- `/wp-json/wc/v3/products` — retrieve related products

Authentication is WordPress username + application password.

## Google Business Profile Integration
`gmb_auth.js` performs OAuth, then retrieves Business Profile account and location IDs. The production publisher uses the local-post endpoint under `mybusiness.googleapis.com`.

Historical implementation status: OAuth/token acquisition worked, but account/location discovery was blocked by Google Cloud quota. Therefore GBP must always be independently re-verified; OAuth success alone does not prove publishing is working.

## SEO / GEO
The permanent rules are documented in `docs/BLOG_PLAYBOOK.md` in the original AI OS repository. Core principles: answer real questions, be factual/useful, use clear headings, add FAQs when useful, link relevant products/internal pages, use a natural CTA, avoid fake claims/hype, and keep business facts consistent. The production SEO gate checks keyword density, title keyword presence, H2 headings and article length; score below 90 blocks the publishing path.

## Duplicate Protection
- `memory/daily_execution_history.json` prevents repeated normal campaign generation on the same day.
- `memory/published_topics.json` maintains the queue and published-topic registry.
- Forced-topic execution intentionally bypasses the normal daily guard.

## Windows Automation
Task name: `AME_Bazaar_Content_Engine`.
A corrected recovery used a daily 09:00 schedule with highest privileges and `C:\Progra~1\nodejs\node.exe`. Historical failure was caused by `schtasks` quoting/admin-permission issues.

## Verification / Debug Order
1. Read `logs/fashion_content_agent.log`.
2. Run `node scripts/verify_agent.js`.
3. Run `node scripts/fashion_content_agent.js --dry-run --verbose`.
4. Check environment-variable presence without exposing values.
5. Check daily history and topic memory.
6. Test WordPress credentials.
7. Test GBP with `node scripts/test_gbp_publish.js`.
8. Only then investigate Windows Task Scheduler.

